# Activity: Axum HTTP Server Architecture, Tracing & Error Handling

## 1. Objective & Context
Establish the foundation for the HTTP REST API in `api/crates/server` using `axum` on top of the `tokio` asynchronous runtime. Configure graceful shutdown, correlation request ID injection, structured request/response tracing via `tower-http`, and centralized RFC 7807 (Problem Details for HTTP APIs) error formatting.

- **Prerequisites:** Feature 01 (Workspace Setup) and `api/crates/core`.
- **Target Location:** `api/crates/server/src/server.rs` and `api/crates/server/src/errors.rs`.

## 2. Technical Scope & Specifications
- **Crate & Version:** `axum` (`0.8.x` or `0.7.x`), `tower-http` (`0.6.x` with `trace`, `request-id`, `cors`, `timeout`), `tokio` (`1.43.x`).
- **Standardized Error Responses:** RFC 7807 JSON structure (`type`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`).
- **Telemetry:** Correlated logs with unique `x-request-id` header on every incoming request.

## 3. Data Structures & Signatures

```rust
use axum::{
    http::StatusCode,
    response::{IntoResponse, Response},
    Json,
};
use serde::Serialize;

#[derive(Debug, Serialize)]
pub struct ProblemDetails {
    pub r#type: String,
    pub title: String,
    pub status: u16,
    pub detail: String,
    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = "Option::is_none")]
    pub instance: Option<String>,
}

#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error)]
pub enum ApiError {
    #[error("Resource not found: {0}")]
    NotFound(String),
    #[error("Validation failed: {0}")]
    BadRequest(String),
    #[error("Unauthorized: {0}")]
    Unauthorized(String),
    #[error("Conflict: {0}")]
    Conflict(String),
    #[error("Internal server error")]
    Internal(#[from] anyhow::Error),
}

impl IntoResponse for ApiError {
    fn into_response(self) -> Response {
        let (status, title, detail) = match &self {
            ApiError::NotFound(msg) => (StatusCode::NOT_FOUND, "Not Found", msg.clone()),
            ApiError::BadRequest(msg) => (StatusCode::BAD_REQUEST, "Bad Request", msg.clone()),
            ApiError::Unauthorized(msg) => (StatusCode::UNAUTHORIZED, "Unauthorized", msg.clone()),
            ApiError::Conflict(msg) => (StatusCode::CONFLICT, "Conflict", msg.clone()),
            ApiError::Internal(err) => {
                tracing::error!(error = ?err, "Internal unhandled error");
                (StatusCode::INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR, "Internal Server Error", "An unexpected error occurred".into())
            }
        };

        let problem = ProblemDetails {
            r#type: format!("https://roubit.app/errors/{}", status.as_u16()),
            title: title.to_string(),
            status: status.as_u16(),
            detail,
            instance: None,
        };

        (status, Json(problem)).into_response()
    }
}
```

## 4. Implementation Steps
1. Add dependencies to `api/crates/server/Cargo.toml`:
   ```toml
   axum = "0.8"
   tower = "0.5"
   tower-http = { version = "0.6", features = ["trace", "request-id", "cors", "timeout"] }
   tokio = { version = "1.43", features = ["full"] }
   ```
2. Implement centralized error responder `api/crates/server/src/errors.rs`.
3. Configure `axum::Router` in `api/crates/server/src/server.rs`:
   - Attach `SetRequestIdLayer` and `PropagateRequestIdLayer`.
   - Attach `TraceLayer::new_for_http()`.
   - Attach `TimeoutLayer::new(Duration::from_secs(30))`.
4. Implement graceful shutdown listening for `SIGINT` / `SIGTERM`.

## 5. Security, Error Handling & Edge Cases
- **No Stack Trace Leaks:** `ApiError::Internal` must log the full internal error to `tracing::error!` for developers while returning a sanitized generic message to the client.
- **Request ID Propagation:** Return `x-request-id` header in the HTTP response so clients can correlate frontend errors with backend server logs.

## 6. Verification & Automated Tests
- Test that unhandled errors return status 500 with RFC 7807 JSON.
- Test that graceful shutdown cleanly drains active connections.

## 7. Definition of Done (DoD)
- [ ] Axum server starts and shuts down cleanly on SIGTERM/Ctrl+C.
- [ ] `TraceLayer` logs requests with correlated request IDs.
- [ ] Error responses strictly conform to RFC 7807 Problem Details.
